1
00:00:13,722 --> 00:00:14,931
This place…

2
00:00:15,015 --> 00:00:18,101
This is Green Dolphin Street Prison!

3
00:00:18,184 --> 00:00:21,354
This is the hallway
by the visitation room!

4
00:00:23,732 --> 00:00:25,108
What the hell do you want?

5
00:00:25,692 --> 00:00:27,360
I don't want to see your face.

6
00:00:27,944 --> 00:00:32,073
It's too late to come
and try to act like a father!

7
00:00:32,699 --> 00:00:34,367
I want to help you.

8
00:00:35,952 --> 00:00:37,495
I'll get you out of here shortly.

9
00:00:37,579 --> 00:00:39,122
Shut up.

10
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:42,417
You know you can't.

11
00:00:43,001 --> 00:00:46,629
I'll serve this two-year sentence
for that hit-and-run and then be released.

12
00:00:47,213 --> 00:00:50,049
Calm down. I've always thought of you--

13
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:54,596
That's a blatant lie.
It's too late to play father figure now.

14
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:55,513
Now leave!

15
00:00:58,349 --> 00:01:00,185
Who are these two?

16
00:01:00,685 --> 00:01:02,729
They look so similar…

17
00:01:02,812 --> 00:01:04,647
to the Joestars!

18
00:01:04,731 --> 00:01:05,732
But it's not them.

19
00:01:05,815 --> 00:01:09,319
Leave! I can't get along with you.

20
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:11,988
What is going on?

21
00:01:12,739 --> 00:01:15,200
Wasn't I at Cape Canaveral?

22
00:01:15,992 --> 00:01:17,994
And what's going on?

23
00:01:18,661 --> 00:01:20,580
What year am I in?

24
00:01:20,663 --> 00:01:25,001
It's 2011, November 30th.

25
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:34,010
Pucchi!

26
00:01:38,056 --> 00:01:39,224
Who the hell are you?

27
00:01:39,307 --> 00:01:41,392
Even a priest isn't allowed
to disrupt a visitation--

28
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:46,314
It's 2011?

29
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:48,358
Did time rewind?

30
00:01:48,942 --> 00:01:50,068
On the contrary.

31
00:01:50,568 --> 00:01:53,071
We leapt through

32
00:01:53,655 --> 00:01:56,991
to the ultimate time
beyond the acceleration.

33
00:01:57,075 --> 00:01:59,160
We went beyond the end of our universe.

34
00:02:00,912 --> 00:02:04,916
The ending of one universe brings about
the beginning of the next.

35
00:02:04,999 --> 00:02:09,420
This is an inevitable truth,
and in the forthcoming universe,

36
00:02:09,504 --> 00:02:13,842
the Earth is created, and living things
experience a life similar to the previous.

37
00:02:13,925 --> 00:02:18,012
The human race went beyond the end
and now faces the dawn of a new start.

38
00:02:18,596 --> 00:02:22,517
This is the new world

39
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,936
Maiden Heaven has promised!

40
00:02:26,187 --> 00:02:28,690
What are you saying?

41
00:02:28,773 --> 00:02:33,027
There's no Jolyne Cujoh in this world.

42
00:02:33,111 --> 00:02:36,114
Neither are there Jotaro,
Anastasia, or Ermes.

43
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:38,408
Even their souls ceased to exist.

44
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:42,036
The dead cannot be brought over.

45
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:44,581
Those who lost their lives
during the time acceleration

46
00:02:44,664 --> 00:02:46,457
have been weeded out of the cycle.

47
00:02:47,083 --> 00:02:51,337
I left behind all my enemies
in the prior universe.

48
00:02:51,921 --> 00:02:54,966
Except for you, Emporio!

49
00:02:55,049 --> 00:02:58,094
You should not have made it over.

50
00:02:58,177 --> 00:03:01,723
You must be ended, here and now!

51
00:04:41,906 --> 00:04:46,703
EPISODE 38: IT'S A WONDERFUL WORLD

52
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:48,997
Code 909. Security Level 4.

53
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:51,541
Visitation room door alarm activated.

54
00:04:51,624 --> 00:04:53,835
Code 909. Security Level 4.

55
00:04:54,669 --> 00:04:55,837
What's going on?

56
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:58,298
Who knows, but now's our chance. Let's go.

57
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:01,968
They're leaving the room
just like Jolyne and Jotaro did.

58
00:05:02,051 --> 00:05:04,971
They're different people,
but the same thing is happening!

59
00:05:05,054 --> 00:05:06,848
This is fate.

60
00:05:06,931 --> 00:05:08,182
This universe

61
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:12,520
has been through the same history
as that of the prior world.

62
00:05:12,603 --> 00:05:14,188
It will remain in the same course.

63
00:05:14,272 --> 00:05:20,194
Fate is brought on by necessity,
not chance.

64
00:05:20,278 --> 00:05:24,532
Now, you're going to
try to find refuge in your room.

65
00:05:25,116 --> 00:05:28,703
I'm talking about your old secret room

66
00:05:28,786 --> 00:05:30,663
that you used to hide in
back in the prior world.

67
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:36,294
Your next actions
are written in your destiny.

68
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:45,762
I have to go somewhere
other than the ghost room!

69
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:49,140
How did prisoners get inside
the general area?

70
00:05:49,223 --> 00:05:51,350
Who knows? Just run.

71
00:05:51,434 --> 00:05:53,644
Those guards are from earlier.

72
00:05:54,228 --> 00:05:55,146
They're going to trip over.

73
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:57,273
What is it?

74
00:05:57,857 --> 00:05:59,734
- We'll trip over.
- What?

75
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:04,238
We keep running in this direction,
and we'll trip over ourselves horribly.

76
00:06:04,322 --> 00:06:06,574
Huh? What the hell are you on about?

77
00:06:07,158 --> 00:06:11,162
That's odd. Why did I think of that?

78
00:06:11,245 --> 00:06:14,082
I don't know, it just came to me.
We're going to trip over.

79
00:06:14,165 --> 00:06:15,583
Are you chickening out?

80
00:06:15,666 --> 00:06:17,960
If we don't hurry, they'll cut our pay!

81
00:06:18,044 --> 00:06:19,587
- Why?
- Right!

82
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:21,631
For some reason, I know.

83
00:06:21,714 --> 00:06:23,841
Those two are about to…

84
00:06:32,350 --> 00:06:33,643
Father!

85
00:06:34,227 --> 00:06:35,103
- What's the matter?
- Move.

86
00:06:39,482 --> 00:06:42,401
No one can escape fate.

87
00:06:42,485 --> 00:06:44,987
You will escape to that room.

88
00:06:54,372 --> 00:06:57,166
What exactly is going on?

89
00:06:57,708 --> 00:07:00,294
We leapt through

90
00:07:00,378 --> 00:07:03,881
to the ultimate time
beyond the acceleration.

91
00:07:05,007 --> 00:07:06,884
We went beyond the end of our universe.

92
00:07:07,468 --> 00:07:08,845
The end of our universe?

93
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:11,514
I've read it in a book once.

94
00:07:12,098 --> 00:07:13,850
How the universe begins and ends.

95
00:07:15,726 --> 00:07:18,646
From the moment it is born,
a universe infinitely expands.

96
00:07:18,729 --> 00:07:20,815
But at a certain point in time,
it begins to contract.

97
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:23,985
Like a stress ball being squeezed,

98
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:27,155
there's a point of singularity
where it can no longer contract.

99
00:07:27,238 --> 00:07:28,865
That marks the end of the universe.

100
00:07:29,365 --> 00:07:35,329
The force leads to a Big Bang,
forming a brand new universe.

101
00:07:36,164 --> 00:07:39,792
Did we come from our world to this one?

102
00:07:40,376 --> 00:07:45,047
Did we travel through Earth's history
at an incredible speed,

103
00:07:45,798 --> 00:07:48,801
and now we're in the new 2011?

104
00:07:49,802 --> 00:07:51,679
But not everyone made it.

105
00:07:52,221 --> 00:07:54,640
The dead cannot be brought over.

106
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:57,518
Those who lost their lives
during the time acceleration

107
00:07:57,602 --> 00:07:59,979
have been weeded out of the cycle.

108
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:05,485
They're gone.

109
00:08:06,819 --> 00:08:10,323
Jolyne and everyone,
they're not part of this world.

110
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:21,709
I've become alone again.

111
00:08:22,835 --> 00:08:26,339
Blessed are those who leapt through time.

112
00:08:28,674 --> 00:08:30,676
They've experienced everything
that is to come

113
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:33,638
and have arrived in this new universe.

114
00:08:34,138 --> 00:08:38,017
This is the world
where fate is predestined.

115
00:08:38,643 --> 00:08:41,354
Fate will repeat itself.

116
00:08:41,938 --> 00:08:44,357
When people meet, it's like gravity.

117
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:46,943
Fate dictates one to meet another.

118
00:08:47,443 --> 00:08:50,613
For example,
what lies five years in the future?

119
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:54,325
Having gone through the accelerated time,

120
00:08:54,408 --> 00:08:57,036
we know what will happen.

121
00:08:57,119 --> 00:09:01,123
When do accidents happen,
and when do we fall ill?

122
00:09:01,832 --> 00:09:03,751
When will our life end?

123
00:09:05,086 --> 00:09:07,797
When do we meet, and when do we part?

124
00:09:08,297 --> 00:09:11,842
When and who do we love and hate?

125
00:09:11,926 --> 00:09:17,056
When do we have children,
and what lies in their future?

126
00:09:18,432 --> 00:09:22,436
When do wars break out,
and when does a new era begin?

127
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:25,856
As if watching a movie,
the future events play out in our minds.

128
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:29,569
So shall it be for our children,
and their posterity!

129
00:09:30,486 --> 00:09:33,531
The time acceleration started
at Cape Canaveral.

130
00:09:33,614 --> 00:09:36,826
Every living being that
lived through this acceleration

131
00:09:36,909 --> 00:09:39,161
can recall the future.

132
00:09:39,245 --> 00:09:42,623
It won't be with their mind or body,
but with their soul!

133
00:09:43,874 --> 00:09:46,627
And that in itself is
the meaning of happiness,

134
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:49,505
because now,
we can prepare for the future.

135
00:09:50,423 --> 00:09:53,259
Blessed are those who prepared!

136
00:09:53,342 --> 00:09:58,389
One may say that to learn of
a bleak future will bring despair.

137
00:09:58,472 --> 00:09:59,599
I say otherwise.

138
00:10:00,182 --> 00:10:02,310
Should you die tomorrow,

139
00:10:02,393 --> 00:10:04,645
the mere knowledge of
what is to come brings peace.

140
00:10:05,521 --> 00:10:08,399
Preparation overcomes despair.

141
00:10:08,482 --> 00:10:10,735
Humanity will evolve.

142
00:10:10,818 --> 00:10:16,741
This is the path to heaven
Dio and I sought to achieve!

143
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:19,493
This is Maiden Heaven.

144
00:10:23,581 --> 00:10:25,249
The gun! My gun!

145
00:10:26,459 --> 00:10:28,461
I dropped it in the ocean!

146
00:10:31,297 --> 00:10:35,676
If I turn right and go down the stairs,
I'll get to my ghost room.

147
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:38,387
But Pucchi already knows
about the secret room.

148
00:10:39,138 --> 00:10:40,640
I shouldn't turn right.

149
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:43,809
I'll turn left and find another place.

150
00:11:01,327 --> 00:11:06,624
Some details may vary,
but you cannot change fate.

151
00:11:07,249 --> 00:11:11,003
Your only option
is to escape into that crack.

152
00:11:16,676 --> 00:11:21,263
Suppose I spare your life
and you go off on your way.

153
00:11:21,764 --> 00:11:24,767
Eventually, you will stand against me.

154
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:26,852
That's the destined future.

155
00:11:27,436 --> 00:11:30,356
I must eliminate you here and now.

156
00:11:30,981 --> 00:11:34,819
Even without Jolyne,
you'll break out of here.

157
00:11:34,902 --> 00:11:39,156
Fate dictates that I lose you
at Cape Canaveral.

158
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:43,577
But here in this prison,
before the acceleration starts,

159
00:11:43,661 --> 00:11:46,455
I know exactly what you'll do.

160
00:11:46,539 --> 00:11:50,334
This is my chance
to eradicate an opposing force.

161
00:11:50,418 --> 00:11:54,171
Hence, I slowed time down on this date.

162
00:11:54,255 --> 00:11:56,090
Prepare to meet your end.

163
00:11:56,173 --> 00:11:59,301
Bracing for the inevitable
brings joy, Emporio.

164
00:12:06,308 --> 00:12:07,685
You are our hope!

165
00:12:11,772 --> 00:12:14,233
Your death shall serve humanity!

166
00:12:15,317 --> 00:12:16,735
Die now, Emporio!

167
00:12:31,208 --> 00:12:33,836
Fate is predestined and can't be changed?

168
00:12:34,795 --> 00:12:36,046
Then…

169
00:12:36,922 --> 00:12:39,091
I'll let you change my fate.

170
00:12:40,426 --> 00:12:45,473
Your arm inserted it into my head
when you punched me into the crack.

171
00:12:47,892 --> 00:12:50,102
When you killed Weather,

172
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:53,397
he extracted his ability,
Weather Forecast, in a disc.

173
00:12:53,481 --> 00:12:56,442
Jolyne wanted me to have it.

174
00:12:56,525 --> 00:12:59,487
She gave me this disc!

175
00:13:06,327 --> 00:13:08,412
Perish in the name of God!

176
00:13:09,079 --> 00:13:11,499
Emporio, your futile actions…

177
00:13:11,582 --> 00:13:16,545
You've merely turned your screams
into the trumpets of hell!

178
00:13:16,629 --> 00:13:19,882
Yes, the ability is now yours.

179
00:13:19,965 --> 00:13:23,219
However, Weather was skilled
in using his power!

180
00:13:23,802 --> 00:13:27,723
It's not an ability you can master
by simply inserting it in your head!

181
00:13:28,390 --> 00:13:29,433
And now!

182
00:13:30,768 --> 00:13:32,228
Time…

183
00:13:32,311 --> 00:13:35,397
accelerates once again!

184
00:13:35,481 --> 00:13:38,776
Learn your feeble place, Emporio…

185
00:13:38,859 --> 00:13:43,405
in the face of my grand purpose!

186
00:13:58,587 --> 00:14:00,881
What?

187
00:14:03,092 --> 00:14:05,761
What is the meaning of this?

188
00:14:06,512 --> 00:14:08,430
I cannot… stand!

189
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:10,224
Something is terribly wrong.

190
00:14:10,307 --> 00:14:12,643
What is this?

191
00:14:14,144 --> 00:14:16,814
Weather Forecast!

192
00:14:17,398 --> 00:14:19,233
I read it in a book once.

193
00:14:19,733 --> 00:14:24,196
Oxygen is the most prevalent toxin
that surrounds living organisms.

194
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:27,366
Yes, living beings need oxygen to live,

195
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:31,912
but it can't surpass 40% saturation.

196
00:14:31,996 --> 00:14:35,207
Pure oxygen is highly toxic.

197
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:37,418
Organisms will die
if they are exposed to it!

198
00:14:38,002 --> 00:14:41,922
In high concentrations, oxygen causes
steel to rust within seconds.

199
00:14:42,006 --> 00:14:43,465
It causes fire to combust,

200
00:14:43,549 --> 00:14:46,552
and robs human cells of electrons!

201
00:14:46,635 --> 00:14:49,138
It destroys the body's organ systems
one at a time!

202
00:14:49,722 --> 00:14:52,641
Inhale pure oxygen,
and your limbs will become paralyzed.

203
00:14:52,725 --> 00:14:54,643
Soon, you lose the ability to stand.

204
00:14:54,727 --> 00:14:58,063
The veins in the eyes burst,
causing blindness.

205
00:14:58,147 --> 00:15:00,608
Acceleration of time is irrelevant.

206
00:15:01,191 --> 00:15:04,361
Weather Forecast is an ability
that manipulates weather.

207
00:15:04,445 --> 00:15:08,073
I was already filling this room
with pure oxygen.

208
00:15:08,157 --> 00:15:10,284
Gradually, you'll lose consciousness.

209
00:15:10,868 --> 00:15:14,705
Pure oxygen will seep into your organs.

210
00:15:15,289 --> 00:15:18,542
Pesky brat…

211
00:15:18,626 --> 00:15:20,544
I'm not controlling this Stand.

212
00:15:20,628 --> 00:15:23,047
This is Weather's ability you sealed away.

213
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:25,758
First, you stole Weather's memories.

214
00:15:25,841 --> 00:15:29,094
Then you awakened this power
along with the snail metamorphosis.

215
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:32,848
Pucchi, you caused your own demise.

216
00:15:34,099 --> 00:15:36,477
Gravity brings one to another.

217
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:39,271
You couldn't cut this force
out of your life!

218
00:15:42,775 --> 00:15:44,693
Stop this, Emporio!

219
00:15:44,777 --> 00:15:46,403
Stop Weather!

220
00:15:46,487 --> 00:15:48,530
Don't make him do this!

221
00:15:48,614 --> 00:15:53,869
I finally attained the will of God!

222
00:15:53,953 --> 00:15:56,830
It is God's will that I use my ability!

223
00:15:57,498 --> 00:16:02,211
With the beginning of the new universe,
humanity can be saved at last!

224
00:16:02,294 --> 00:16:04,630
In this world,
we haven't reached Cape Canaveral,

225
00:16:04,713 --> 00:16:07,383
where I acquired time acceleration.

226
00:16:07,466 --> 00:16:09,635
Maiden Heaven is still incomplete.

227
00:16:10,302 --> 00:16:14,139
I will gladly offer my life
after Cape Canaveral.

228
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:15,474
If I die,

229
00:16:15,557 --> 00:16:19,228
everything I've accomplished
will be undone!

230
00:16:19,311 --> 00:16:22,606
You will change humanity's fate!

231
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:26,944
Then people will no longer know
what will happen in the future,

232
00:16:27,027 --> 00:16:29,196
and they won't be able to
prepare for the inevitable.

233
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:33,367
Remember,
preparation brings true happiness!

234
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:38,038
I refuse to die here!

235
00:16:38,622 --> 00:16:39,873
Don't you understand?

236
00:16:40,541 --> 00:16:42,710
You've already been defeated by fate.

237
00:16:42,793 --> 00:16:44,420
Stop talking nonsense, child!

238
00:16:44,503 --> 00:16:46,505
Realize that I didn't do this alone.

239
00:16:46,588 --> 00:16:50,009
You've also been defeated by Jolyne,
who sent me here.

240
00:16:50,592 --> 00:16:51,719
Weather.

241
00:16:51,802 --> 00:16:52,803
F.F.

242
00:16:52,886 --> 00:16:53,971
Ermes.

243
00:16:54,054 --> 00:16:55,139
Anastasia.

244
00:16:55,222 --> 00:16:57,224
And even Jotaro.

245
00:16:57,808 --> 00:17:00,853
They didn't know what lies ahead,
but they all had resolve.

246
00:17:01,729 --> 00:17:05,232
You're the one who's unprepared, Pucchi!

247
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:09,737
Walking the path of justice
is fate itself!

248
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:12,114
Stop this now!

249
00:17:12,197 --> 00:17:16,326
Stop spewing nonsense
as if you understand!

250
00:17:18,162 --> 00:17:21,749
You insignificant brat!

251
00:18:25,646 --> 00:18:26,647
It's a bus.

252
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:29,942
Like I said,

253
00:18:30,025 --> 00:18:32,986
I only have 50 dollars!

254
00:18:33,070 --> 00:18:35,864
What kind of bus doesn't have change?

255
00:18:37,324 --> 00:18:38,158
What?

256
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:40,994
- Is that how you talk to a customer?
- Good, the bus stopped.

257
00:18:41,078 --> 00:18:43,330
All right, give me a moment.

258
00:18:43,413 --> 00:18:46,041
I'll break it for some change
at the gas station.

259
00:18:47,292 --> 00:18:49,753
Hey kid, are you getting on this bus?

260
00:18:49,837 --> 00:18:52,214
Good timing, got any spare change on you?

261
00:18:53,173 --> 00:18:54,925
I need to break this 50-dollar bill.

262
00:18:55,008 --> 00:18:56,760
Please?

263
00:18:56,844 --> 00:18:58,804
It's not counterfeit.

264
00:18:58,887 --> 00:19:00,389
What? Hey!

265
00:19:00,472 --> 00:19:02,224
Wait up, jerk!

266
00:19:02,307 --> 00:19:04,601
He tossed my bag out, dammit!

267
00:19:06,228 --> 00:19:10,566
The bus left because
you were taking your time!

268
00:19:10,649 --> 00:19:13,861
The next bus is in two hours.
What am I going to do?

269
00:19:13,944 --> 00:19:15,612
You listening?

270
00:19:16,613 --> 00:19:17,698
Dammit.

271
00:19:18,282 --> 00:19:19,658
Whatever.

272
00:19:19,741 --> 00:19:23,287
Maybe he thought
I was a Green Dolphin jailbreak.

273
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:25,539
You're…

274
00:19:25,622 --> 00:19:27,040
What?

275
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:31,086
Hey. My car's out of gas.

276
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:36,925
If you pay for my gas and meals,
I'll take you anywhere.

277
00:19:37,426 --> 00:19:39,094
What do you say, kid?

278
00:19:39,678 --> 00:19:42,306
That how you pinch trip money?

279
00:19:42,389 --> 00:19:46,685
My sis always said
not to ride with a stranger.

280
00:19:52,399 --> 00:19:55,068
See, a storm is coming.

281
00:19:55,569 --> 00:19:58,488
You're free to test your luck

282
00:19:59,489 --> 00:20:01,325
and see if you can stay dry
until the next bus.

283
00:20:09,333 --> 00:20:12,920
Hop in, kid. We won't bite.

284
00:20:14,963 --> 00:20:16,548
I'm Irene.

285
00:20:16,632 --> 00:20:18,175
He's Anakiss.

286
00:20:18,842 --> 00:20:20,427
Where are your parents?

287
00:20:21,094 --> 00:20:24,264
We're going to see my father.

288
00:20:26,308 --> 00:20:27,434
This guy is…

289
00:20:28,268 --> 00:20:29,686
my boyfriend.

290
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:36,485
Who knows how Father will react,
but if he gives us his blessing,

291
00:20:36,568 --> 00:20:39,863
we might get married.

292
00:20:41,865 --> 00:20:44,993
Damn, you sure about the storm?

293
00:20:45,077 --> 00:20:47,955
Ten dollars is all you're getting from me,

294
00:20:48,038 --> 00:20:51,124
and make a stop at Cape Canaveral,
got that?

295
00:20:51,208 --> 00:20:54,086
Hop in. I can use your help.

296
00:20:54,169 --> 00:20:56,880
Honestly, it helps me too.

297
00:20:57,464 --> 00:20:58,966
Are you okay, kid?

298
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:02,344
What's your name?

299
00:21:05,514 --> 00:21:07,391
Don't be shy. Hop on.

300
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:13,355
We won't ask for money.

301
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:16,108
You're shaking.

302
00:21:16,692 --> 00:21:17,901
Are you cold?

303
00:21:18,485 --> 00:21:19,319
Here.

304
00:21:22,155 --> 00:21:23,782
I'm…

305
00:21:26,451 --> 00:21:27,786
Emporio.

306
00:21:29,371 --> 00:21:31,164
That's my name.

307
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:36,670
My name… is Emporio.

308
00:21:49,558 --> 00:21:51,852
Look, a hitchhiker.

309
00:21:51,935 --> 00:21:55,397
No more. Two is enough.

310
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:58,066
You said the storm is coming.

311
00:21:58,150 --> 00:22:00,736
Stop the car, we can't leave him.

312
00:22:13,081 --> 00:22:20,088
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE - STONE OCEAN
THE END

313
00:23:47,884 --> 00:23:52,889
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
